<%# One application's CI, drawn as a testing card: the check meter on top, then the
    branch ladder as badges beneath it.

    THE METER is components/_ci_progress_meter, the same one the board card and the
    Next Release card already use — one mark per check inside a rail (✓ passed,
    ✗ failed, a spinner while running) with a clock that ticks live and freezes to the
    run's duration when it settles. Reusing it rather than drawing a second kind of
    meter is the point: the operator learns this vocabulary once, and a check here
    means what a check means everywhere else on the page.

    IT REPORTS ON ONE RUNG — Card#active_rung: a running suite if there is one, else
    the newest verdict. Three check-lists on one card is the two-rows-saying-the-same-
    thing shape the CI meter already collapsed once.

    THE BADGES say where each rung stands, and read left to right as the ladder:
      faded   — NOT BUILT. Nothing ingested for this branch, so there is no verdict
                to report. An absence must never read as a pass.
      amber   — running.
      emerald — green.
      rose    — failed or conflicted.

    A badge reports CI's verdict and adds nothing to it. It used to also carry a
    `stale` state, inferred from stamp timestamps; that inference was wrong by
    construction and is gone — see Ci::LadderRung.

    THE WHOLE CARD IS A LINK to the Actions run behind the active rung, so a click
    lands on the run in progress. When there is no run to open it degrades to a plain
    <div> — never a dead link, the same rule tasks/_release_phase_meter follows.

    Locals:
      card       - Ci::AppLadder::Card
      card_class - extra classes for the grid cell %>
<% card = local_assigns.fetch(:card) %>
<% attention = card.needs_attention? %>
<% progress = card.progress %>
<% run_url = card.run_url %>
<% linked = run_url.present? %>

<% card_classes = ["rounded-xl border bg-surface p-4 block min-w-0 transition-colors",
                   attention ? "border-amber-500/40" : "border-subtle",
                   local_assigns[:card_class]].compact.join(" ") %>
<% card_classes += " group hover:border-primary/50 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary" if linked %>
<% card_options = {
     class: card_classes,
     data: { test: "app-ladder-card", repo: card.repo, attention: attention, linked: linked },
     title: linked ? "#{card.repo} — open the GitHub Actions run for #{card.active_rung&.branch}" : card.repo
   } %>
<% if linked %>
  <% card_options.merge!(href: run_url, target: "_blank", rel: "noopener") %>
<% end %>

<%= content_tag(linked ? :a : :div, **card_options) do %>
  <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-2 mb-2 min-w-0">
    <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold truncate"><%= card.repo %></h3>
    <span class="flex items-center gap-1 shrink-0 text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-muted">
      <%= card.gem? ? "gem" : "app" %>
      <%# The affordance: an arrow that surfaces on hover, so the card reads as
          clickable without a permanent chrome element competing with the meter. %>
      <% if linked %>
        <span class="opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      <% end %>
    </span>
  </div>

  <%# The CI meter. Rendered only when checks were actually ingested — an absent
      suite must not draw an empty rail that reads as "0 of 0 passed". %>
  <% if progress.present? %>
    <div class="mb-2.5" data-test="app-ladder-ci">
      <%# The label NAMES the lane, not a generic "CI". On a multi-lane repo the meter
          counts one workflow by design, so saying which one is what stops a reader
          assuming it covers everything — the assumption that let a green meter sit
          beside a red badge. %>
      <%= render "components/ci_progress_meter",
            progress: progress,
            label: [card.active_rung&.branch, card.active_rung&.counted_lane].compact.join(" · "),
            test_id: "app-ladder-ci-bar",
            clock: true %>
    </div>
  <% else %>
    <div class="mb-2.5 rounded border border-dashed border-subtle px-2 py-2 text-[10px] text-muted"
         data-test="app-ladder-ci-empty">
      no CI checks ingested for this app yet
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <%# THE OTHER LANES. The badge folds every workflow on the sha; the meter folds one.
      Rather than force those to agree — they answer different questions, and the
      meter's scope protects a gem's track from a failing consumer — the card NAMES
      what the meter leaves out. A red sibling lane is then visible here instead of
      hiding behind a green meter, which is the contradiction this row shipped with.
      Empty for every single-lane repo, so an app card gains nothing to read. %>
  <% others = card.active_rung&.uncounted_lanes || [] %>
  <% if others.any? %>
    <div class="mb-2.5 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 text-[10px]"
         data-test="app-ladder-other-lanes">
      <span class="text-muted">also on this commit:</span>
      <% others.each do |lane| %>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 <%= app_ladder_rung_tone(lane[:state])[:text] %>"
              data-test="app-ladder-other-lane"
              data-lane="<%= lane[:name] %>"
              data-state="<%= lane[:state] %>"
              title="<%= lane[:name] %> — <%= lane[:state] == :green ? "passed" : lane[:state] == :red ? "failed" : "running" %>; not counted by the meter above">
          <span aria-hidden="true"><%= lane[:state] == :green ? "✓" : lane[:state] == :red ? "✗" : "○" %></span>
          <span><%= lane[:name] %></span>
        </span>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <%# The ladder badges, under the meter. %>
  <div class="flex items-stretch gap-1"
       data-test="app-ladder-suite"
       role="group"
       aria-label="<%= app_ladder_suite_summary(card) %>">
    <% Ci::AppLadder::RUNGS.each do |branch| %>
      <% rung = card.rung(branch) %>
      <% next if rung.blank? %>
      <% tone = app_ladder_rung_tone(rung.state) %>
      <div class="relative flex-1 min-w-0 overflow-hidden rounded border <%= tone[:border] %> bg-inset"
           data-test="app-ladder-rung"
           data-branch="<%= branch %>"
           data-state="<%= rung.state %>"
           title="<%= app_ladder_rung_title(rung) %>">
        <%# A TINT, never a solid block — the label rides on top of it. Same 15/30
            split the release meter measured at 5.3:1 or better in both themes. %>
        <div class="absolute inset-0 <%= tone[:fill] %> opacity-15 dark:opacity-30"
             data-test="app-ladder-rung-fill"></div>
        <div class="relative flex items-center justify-center gap-1 px-1.5 py-1 <%= tone[:text] %>">
          <% if rung.state == :pending %>
            <svg class="h-2 w-2 shrink-0 animate-spin motion-reduce:animate-none" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
              <circle class="opacity-25" cx="12" cy="12" r="9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"/>
              <path class="opacity-90" d="M12 3a9 9 0 0 1 9 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"/>
            </svg>
          <% elsif rung.state == :green %>
            <svg class="h-2 w-2 shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="4" d="M4.5 12.75l6 6 9-13.5"/>
            </svg>
          <% elsif %i[red conflicted].include?(rung.state) %>
            <svg class="h-2 w-2 shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="4" d="M6 18 18 6M6 6l12 12"/>
            </svg>
          <% end %>
          <span class="truncate text-[10px] font-medium leading-none"><%= branch %></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <%# Parked work — how many tasks sit at each rung right now. Derived from the
      board's `merged` column, so it drains on its own as a sweep and then a ship
      advance the stamps. %>
  <% parked = Ci::AppLadder::RUNGS.filter_map { |b| [b, card.rung(b)&.parked_count.to_i] if card.rung(b)&.parked_count.to_i&.positive? } %>
  <% if parked.any? %>
    <div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-x-3 gap-y-0.5 text-[10px] text-muted" data-test="app-ladder-parked-row">
      <% parked.each do |branch, count| %>
        <span data-test="app-ladder-parked" data-branch="<%= branch %>">
          <span class="tabular-nums font-medium"><%= count %></span> on <%= branch %>
        </span>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
